{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397968,"nonce":"o63FPy8wWwygh79Ut/OcrAUawfQ=","title":"LSP compiles synchronously on every keystroke, with no cancellation or incremental sync","message":"The server is a single loop (`lsp/src/server.rs:108`). Every `didChange` builds a new `CompilationUnit`, loads the stdlib and lowers to TAST before the next message is read. Sync is FULL text. There is no `$/cancelRequest` handling, debounce or background worker. Today the compile takes about 0.03 s on a 10-line file, so it does not show yet, but it grows with the project and the class paths.\n\nNeeded:\n- incremental text sync;\n- a debounced background compile;\n- keeping the last good analysis for queries while a new one runs;\n- reuse of the loaded stdlib between compiles instead of reloading it each time.","files":null}]}